<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">La Tadampare Puang ri Ma'galatung</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">La Tadampare Puang ri Ma'galatung was an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arung-matoa">Arung Matoa</a>, or elected ruler, of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bugis">Bugis</a> kingdom of Wajo in South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulawesi">Sulawesi</a> around the turn of the 16th century. Bugis chronicles remember him as Wajo's wisest ruler, a statesman whose sayings on government, justice and the rights of the people of Wajo were preserved and quoted for centuries. Under his rule Wajo grew in power among the Bugis states.</p></div>
